  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Speeding up of Universal Access to Prevention, Treament and Support Services - Congo (Democratic Republic) (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Congo (Democratic Republic), Tuberculosis, Ministry of Public Health, Hygiene and Social Security (MOH DRC)This program has the following goals: Contribute to the reduction of 25% of TB related mortality by 2025.  Ensure global care and treatment of all TB/HIV co-infected patients in DRC. The objectives of this program are: Detect by 2017 387,785 TB cases all forms in DRC.  Enrol 95% of TB/HIV co-infected patients on ART by 2017.  Maintain treatment success rate for bacteriologically confirmed cases of at least 90%.  Treat successfully 75% of MDR-TB patients by 2017 (long regimen)</narrative>
  </description>
